---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { buildGraph } from '../lib/schema';
import { companyLine, publisherLine, publishingStatement, site } from '../data/site';
import { formatDate } from '../lib/format';

const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { label: 'About', href: '/about/' },
];
const updated = new Date(`${site.policiesUpdated}T00:00:00.000Z`);
const description = 'Creator Rogenie founded 9nth Dimension. This desk explains Super Intelligence (SI), still called AI, from public sources. We sell the Family AI Safety Kit, and we say so.';
---
<Base title={`About · ${site.name}`} description={description} graph={buildGraph({ crumbs })}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="kicker">The desk</p>
    <h1>About this desk</h1>
    <p class="lede">Ancient name. Modern nonsense detector. The Latin means “ancient intelligence,” and the standard is simple: show the document, or do not say it.</p>
    <p>{companyLine}</p>
    <p class="meta">Updated <time datetime={site.policiesUpdated}>{formatDate(updated)}</time></p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="research-desk">Who runs this</h2>
    <p>
      Creator Rogenie founded {site.company}. Intelligentia Antiqua is one of her companies, and the voice is hers: direct, exact, a little amused by a pitch that will not show its work, and serious about the person reading. Your time, your choices, and your mind are the point.
    </p>
    <p>
      The audience is a complete beginner. A parent. A worker. An owner of a small business. Anyone who wants to understand the tool before trusting it with a decision. Curiosity is welcome here. Condescension is not.
    </p>
    <p>
      The desk leads with <a href="/glossary/#super-intelligence">Super Intelligence (SI), still widely called AI</a>. Quotations, source titles, and product names stay in their own words. The Family AI Safety Kit keeps its name.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Intelligentia Antiqua Research Desk writes the guides in that voice. The desk is not a law firm, a medical practice, a financial adviser, or a university. Reading a page does not make you a client, and it does not make the desk your expert.
    </p>
    <p>{publishingStatement} Creator Rogenie does not pretend to re-read every merge by hand. The gate is real. A personal signature on every file is not.</p>
    <p>
      {publisherLine}. Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Please do not send passwords, medical records, or copies of an ID.
    </p>
    <h2 id="funding">How we are funded</h2>
    <p>
      No lab pays for coverage. We do not sell ads on the guides. We do not use affiliate links today. If we add one, the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> will name the relationship before the link goes live, and the page will say so next to the link.
    </p>
    <p>
      We sell the <a href="/safety-kit/">Family AI Safety Kit</a>: 4 write-in family code-word wallet cards, a large-print fridge magnet with the call-back steps, 6 sliding webcam covers, and a setup card. We have a financial interest in that kit. The kit page says so at the top, and any guide that mentions the kit says so beside the mention. Pre-orders are open on that page. A charge shows as {site.cardStatement}, because {site.name} is a {site.company} company.
    </p>
    <p>
      Editorial stays separate from that product. We choose topics because a beginner needs them. Guides cite their sources. No article requires a purchase. The <a href="/articles/ai-scams-voice-clones-and-deepfakes/">voice-clone guide</a> is the free method. The cards are a convenience.
    </p>
    <h2>What we will not do</h2>
    <p>We will not tell you a chatbot is correct. We will not invent a statistic, a victim, or a quote. We will not hide a correction. We will not sand a disagreement into a slogan because a slogan is easier to share. A polished claim that cannot point at a page does not get repeated here.</p>
    <p>The <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> is the longer version of those rules. The <a href="/sourcing/">sourcing page</a> lists which documents we trust first.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
